// run_capped, spawning a real ("true") child under no limits with real
// stdout/stderr streams, is the sole exporter of cr_h/cr_out/cr_err
// (main.id): nothing else may declare them, so this is the only way any
// other case gets a real (if, by the time this returns, already drained and
// closed) value for cr_h. Reused by every case below that needs one.
ccrun_fx_run_capped_true() {
  int ccrun_fx_rc_code = run_capped("true\n", "-", 0, 0);
} return void;
